# QMD Search for Documentation

This project has 148 markdown docs indexed with QMD (tobi/qmd). Use qmd BEFORE reading files manually - it's faster and finds relevant content across the entire docs/ folder.

## When to Use QMD

- Looking for how a feature works → `qmd search "feature name"`
- Finding API endpoints → `qmd search "endpoint api"`
- Understanding architecture → `qmd search "system architecture"`
- Troubleshooting → `qmd search "error handling"`
- Finding code examples → `qmd search "example python"`

## Commands (in order of speed)

```bash
# 1. FAST keyword search (use first, 90% of the time)
qmd search "canvas pin system" -n 5

# 2. Get structured JSON results (best for parsing)
qmd search "authentication" --json -n 10

# 3. Get full document content after finding it
qmd get "CANVAS_SYSTEM.md" --full

# 4. Semantic search (when keywords don't match)
qmd vsearch "how does jarvis remember things"

# 5. Hybrid with re-ranking (best quality, slowest)
qmd query "error handling" --all --files --min-score 0.4

# 6. List files in a section
qmd ls jarvis-docs/api
```

## Search Options

```bash
-n <num>           # Number of results (default: 5, or 20 for --json)
-c, --collection   # Restrict to collection: -c jarvis-docs
--all              # Return all matches (use with --min-score)
--min-score <num>  # Minimum score threshold (0.0-1.0)
--full             # Show full document content
--line-numbers     # Add line numbers to output

# Output formats
--json             # JSON output with snippets (best for parsing)
--files            # Output: docid,score,filepath,context
--md               # Markdown output
```

## Get Options

```bash
qmd get "file.md" --full      # Full content
qmd get "file.md:50" -l 100   # Start at line 50, max 100 lines
qmd get "#abc123"             # By docid from search results
```

## Key Indexed Sections

- `/api` - REST API endpoints (port 8880)
- `/mcp` - MCP server configs
- `/n8n` - Workflow automation
- `/opencode` - Coding agent
- `/service` - systemd services
- `INTELLIGENCE_LAYER.md` - Orchestration brain
- `MEMORY_SYSTEM.md` - Memory architecture
- `TOOL_MANAGEMENT.md` - 54+ tools list

## Re-indexing (when docs change)

```bash
qmd update                    # Re-index changed files
qmd update --pull             # Git pull first, then re-index
qmd embed                     # Regenerate embeddings after update
```

## Why This Matters

Reading docs directly wastes tokens. QMD finds the exact section needed:
- 148 files × ~500 lines avg = 74,000 lines of docs
- QMD search returns just the relevant snippets
- 33 context annotations improve search relevance
